-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/07/15/rollout-2026-07-15T15-22-01-019f65f1-0246-7c83-9c24-dd45127a4929.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-15T13:44:33+00:00, thread_id=019f65f1-0246-7c83-9c24-dd45127a4929, same rollout; distinct routing value for compile/verification and conditional-closeout guidance)\n1899-\n1900-### keywords\n--\n1935-- symptom: a helper cannot reopen an existing file while updating a workline README in this sandbox -> cause: patch-helper reopening was unreliable in this environment -> fix: be ready to use another non-destructive edit path if the helper cannot reopen the target [Task 1]\n1936-- symptom: `technical.tex` fails on the first compile with an undefined macro -> cause: required math macros such as `\\\\cR` were not defined in the draft preamble -> fix: define custom macros before the first compile and rerun immediately on the exact error [Task 2]\n1937:- symptom: first-pass LaTeX warnings look like unresolved problems at closeout -> cause: references only settle after a second pass -> fix: rerun `pdflatex` and report final-state warnings separately from first-pass noise [Task 2]\n1938-- symptom: visual PDF inspection cannot be completed through the sandboxed image viewer -> cause: rendered PNG paths could not be reopened in this environment -> fix: treat `pdfinfo` plus successful PDF generation as the verified fallback and state that visual inspection remained partial [Task 2]\n1939-- symptom: `P_\\Lambda\\otimes I_{\\Lambda^c}` is called a normalized density matrix -> cause: it is a constraint projector whose trace is generally not one -> fix: for a finite density matrix use `P_F/rank(P_F)`; also ensure any `|S_F|` in a rank formula means the number of independent stabilizers (`log_2|G_F|`), not a redundant generator-list length [Task 3]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
