{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' <original-home>/.codex/memories/rollout_summaries/2026-08-06T14-29-28-EPRR-two_lane_aristotle_autopilot_closeout_hardening.md\"","aggregated_output":"thread_id: 019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677\nupdated_at: 2026-08-06T18:07:30+00:00\nrollout_path: <original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/06/rollout-2026-08-06T16-29-28-019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677.jsonl\ncwd: source-workspace\ngit_branch: master\n\n# Prepared and launched a two-lane Aristotle/Codex overnight formalization loop, then diagnosed closeout failures\n\nRollout context: The user wanted autonomous formalization of two related theorem programs: (1) finite-range stabilizer systems should have no type-III central summands, and (2) systems with coherent local hyperbolic bases should admit a type-I/pure-sector tensor mixed-sector decomposition. The user explicitly allowed Aristotle to develop missing C*/von Neumann/GNS/tensor-product theory or use an easier proof route, provided the resulting theorem is recognizable, added assumptions are explicit, and no axioms/placeholders are used.\n\n## Task 1: Design and prepare the two-lane Aristotle autopilot\n\nOutcome: success\n\nPreference signals:\n- The user asked to \"append the endgame packets and start the loop\" after reviewing the readiness assessment -> future automation work should include endgame packets reaching the actual theorem targets, not stop at conditional infrastructure interfaces.\n- The user clarified that Aristotle may develop necessary theory absent from Mathlib or implicit in the paper and may change the tensor-product proof route -> future packets should permit project-local supporting theory and alternative valid proofs while requiring explicit premises and honest theorem-scope reporting.\n- The user requested only `main.tex` and bibliography files from Overleaf -> upload snapshots should contain `manuscript/main.tex`, `references.bib`, and `mainNotes.bib`, not the whole Overleaf tree.\n\nKey steps:\n- Located the old orchestrator under `work/OLD/formalization/`; determined it was hard-wired to obsolete `MANIFEST.toml`, blueprints, and `Formalization/` paths.\n- Built the replacement under `work/aristotle_autopilot/` with two independent deterministic queues, one active Aristotle task per lane, Codex closeout only after terminal status, and advancement only after machine-readable `AUTOPILOT_ACCEPTED: yes` plus `AUTOPILOT_DECISION: advance`.\n- Queues were extended to finite-fiber `FF15`–`FF23` and stabilizer-hyperfinite `P37`–`P46`, ending in the requested no-type-III central-summand and local-hyperbolic tensor-decomposition targets.\n- Added `AUTONOMY_POLICY.md`: missing C*/von Neumann/GNS/tensor/Pauli theory may be developed; alternative proof routes are allowed; no `sorry`, `admit`, axioms, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or silent weakening.\n- Added compact manuscript staging and verified snapshots contain exactly `main.tex`, `mainNotes.bib`, `references.bib`, plus the autonomy policy.\n- Verified Python compilation, queue-file existence, both project builds, dry-run queue selection, and systemd unit syntax.\n\nReusable knowledge:\n- Live runner: `workflow/aristotle_autopilot.py`.\n- Configuration: `work/aristotle_autopilot/autopilot.toml`.\n- The timer is user-systemd, polling every five minutes; it was enabled at `<original-home>/.config/systemd/user/aristotle-autopilot.timer`.\n- Initial submissions succeeded: FF15 project `ea65520b-e894-4868-8d69-851fde31b30e`, task `f17e2043-2bd3-431a-a76d-8967c9802ef8`; P37 project `9d0fc268-fb0f-4e00-827f-c6b5d7e4ca17`, task `bc90659a-6636-43c6-bd4e-5694a268ad2a`.\n\n## Task 2: Diagnose and repair stalled autonomous closeouts\n\nOutcome: partial\n\nFailures and how to do differently:\n- First failure: systemd could not find Codex because the NVM-installed executable was outside the service PATH (`[Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'codex'`). Aristotle jobs completed, but no Codex closeout ran and queues did not advance. Fix: explicitly set PATH and `AUTOPILOT_CODEX_BIN=<original-home>/.nvm/versions/node/v24.14.0/bin/codex` in the service, and resolve the executable explicitly in Python.\n- Second failure: the first closeout ran Lean builds inside the downloaded quarantine snapshot. Because it lacked `.lake`, Lean cloned Mathlib/dependencies and consumed about 13 GB memory. Fix: inspect/quarantine downloaded artifacts but copy only the candidate into the live project and run all Lean checks in the already-built live checkout.\n- The initial closeout was stopped before completion; the candidate file `formalization_finite_fibers/FiniteFiber/FiniteRegionFullPauliMultiplication.lean` had already been copied into the live project and was preserved.\n- Added persisted closeout metadata before Codex starts. If Codex is interrupted without a machine-readable decision, the lane now halts for review instead of silently retrying or advancing ambiguously.\n\nCurrent status at rollout end:\n- The repaired service was running a finite-fiber Codex closeout with greatly reduced memory (~330 MB initially versus ~13 GB previously), but no final accepted decision had yet been recorded in the supplied rollout. State still showed FF15 and P37 as active; therefore no successor submission was verified in this rollout.\n\nReferences:\n- `work/aristotle_autopilot/aristotle-autopilot.service` now contains explicit Codex PATH/bin settings.\n- `work/aristotle_autopilot/codex_closeout_prompt.md` explicitly forbids building or fetching dependencies inside downloaded archives.\n- `work/aristotle_autopilot/state.json` records active tasks and persisted closeout paths.\n- Exact error: `[Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'codex'`.\n- Codex executable: `<original-home>/.nvm/versions/node/v24.14.0/bin/codex` (`codex-cli 0.146.0`).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
