{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' reviews/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-closeout.md; sed -n '1,280p' reviews/P55B-local-hyperbolic-source-uhf-bridge-closeout.md; sed -n '1,320p' reviews/P55C-local-hyperbolic-concrete-representations-closeout.md\"","aggregated_output":"# P55A closeout review — local-hyperbolic finite-stage UHF bridge\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated infrastructure-only Lane-H scope; queue may\nadvance.**\n\nThe terminal status for Aristotle task\n`2e89017e-ccab-47c2-bd66-ca42164fd972` is `COMPLETE` in\n`history/logs/20260808T161409Z-1ac3c887-tasks.log`.\nIts exact archive\n`aristotle_responses/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-1ac3c887-2e89017e.tar.gz`\nwas extracted only to\n`aristotle_responses/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-1ac3c887-2e89017e-quarantine/`.\nNo build, update, or dependency fetch was run in that dependency-free\nsnapshot.  Only the packet-authorized candidate\n`AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicFiniteStageUHFBridge.lean` was\nintegrated into the live project.  Its live and quarantine SHA-256 values\nagree:\n\n```text\n42b18ef984b2046a4004ae64e8e79a0df7454e0c122b8d9722145bc6e2d28b3a\n```\n\nNo raw response record was integrated: the packet authorizes only the\ncandidate module.  The archive and quarantine extraction are retained as raw\nevidence.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nThe new module imports the accepted P53 module\n`AristotleCandidates.LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha` and\n`Formalization.DyadicTensorTower`; their archived versions are\nbyte-identical to the live versions.  It constructs, rather than receives as\na field:\n\n- `UHFBridge.qubitMatrixEquiv k :\n  QubitTensorPower k ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] Matrix (Reg (Fin k)) (Reg (Fin k)) ℂ`;\n- recursive dyadic words `qubitX`, `qubitZ`, and\n  `qubitWord k a b := qubitX k a * qubitZ k b`;\n- `AlphaData.sourceStageMatrixEquiv n e`, obtained from P53's\n  `pauliWordBasis`, the explicitly proved matrix-word basis\n  `stdWordBasis`, and the supplied enumeration\n  `e : A.Coord n ≃ Fin k`; and\n- the packet target\n\n  ```lean\n  A.sourceStageUHFEquiv n e :\n    pauliAlgebra (A.sourceForm n) ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] QubitTensorPower k\n  ```\n\n  defined by transport through the constructed register-matrix equivalence.\n\nThe exact word and generator formulae are:\n\n```lean\nA.sourceStageUHFEquiv n e (pauliWord (A.sourceForm n) v) =\n  qubitWord k (A.enumRepr n e v).1 (A.enumRepr n e v).2\n\nA.sourceStageUHFEquiv n e\n    (pauliWord (A.sourceForm n) ((A.stageCoordinates n).z i)) =\n  qubitZ k (Pi.single (e i) 1)\n\nA.sourceStageUHFEquiv n e\n    (pauliWord (A.sourceForm n) ((A.stageCoordinates n).x i)) =\n  qubitX k (Pi.single (e i) 1)\n```\n\nThey are exported as `sourceStageUHFEquiv_word`,\n`sourceStageUHFEquiv_zGenerator`, and\n`sourceStageUHFEquiv_xGenerator`, together with\n`sourceStageUHFEquiv_bijective`,\n`sourceStageUHFEquivDefault` at `Nat.card (A.Coord n)`, and\n`norm_sourceStageUHFEquiv`,\n`norm_sourceStageMatrixEquiv`, and\n`isometry_sourceStageMatrixEquiv`.\n\nThe convention check is explicit.  The ordered word is `X^a Z^b`; its\nmultiplication sign is `(-1)^(b dot a')`, its star sign is\n`(-1)^(a dot b)`, and\n`i^(a dot b) X^a Z^b` is proved self-adjoint.  Both coordinate-generator\nimages have trivial fourth-root phase because their respective exponent\npairings vanish.  The recursive tensor convention puts coordinate zero in the\nouter matrix factor through `regSuccEquiv`; no unproved permutation is used.\n\nThere are no new mathematical premises.  The bridge inherits exactly P53's\n`AlphaData` data: a P52 locally supported hyperbolic family and exhaustion,\nplus the explicitly named auxiliary fields `symplectic` and\n`stage_surjective`.  The finite coordinate enumeration is constructed with\n`Finite.equivFin`; classical choice is not a supplied hypothesis.  Since\n`QubitTensorPower k` has no native normed additive structure in the pinned\nAPI, the candidate defines `qubitOpNorm` through the proved register-matrix\nmodel and states the distance-form isometry in that matrix model.  This is an\nexplicit norm-control route, not a hidden C-star completion premise.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | From every explicit enumeration `e`, the finite P53 source Pauli algebra is star-isomorphic to the corresponding recursive `k`-qubit dyadic stage; the word, X/Z-generator, multiplication, star, bijectivity, and induced norm statements are proved. |\n| partial | This is infrastructure only.  It does not construct the manuscript's actual coordinate realization; it inherits P53's named `AlphaData` assumptions and does not identify any direct limit. |\n| blocked | None at the P55A gate. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is met exactly at its stated scope.  The\nsupporting matrix route is not a weakened target: it constructs an explicit\nstar equivalence between the recursive dyadic stage and its finite register\nmatrix model before transporting the explicitly constructed Pauli-word map.\nNo added premise or alternate conditional conclusion was introduced.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P55A, Lane H, as declared in the packet and the active\n  plan.\n- **Predecessors:** P53 only.  Its accepted, locally compiled, semantically\n  audited closeout is\n  `reviews/P53-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha-closeout.md`.  P55A imports\n  that live module and standard checked dyadic infrastructure; it does not\n  use P55B--P55D or an unaccepted remote artifact.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: constructed finite-stage Pauli-to-dyadic\n  star equivalences, explicit generator/phase formulae, and norm control.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected.  No declaration identifies a\n  direct limit, constructs a C-star completion or regional alpha, proves a\n  state identity or GNS split, calls an algebra a factor, or gives a\n  trace/weight conclusion.\n\nNo manuscript source clause is represented by this infrastructure-only\npacket.  In particular, it does not promote the still-unformalized\nshort-range regional-algebra theorem or its analytic tensor-product steps.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.LocalHyperbolicFiniteStageUHFBridge` —\n  passed in the live project (`8050/8050` jobs).\n- `lake build` — passed in the live project.\n- `lake env lean /dev/stdin` importing the live candidate and printing the\n  axioms of `sourceStageUHFEquiv`,\n  `sourceStageUHFEquiv_zGenerator`,\n  `sourceStageUHFEquiv_xGenerator`,\n  `sourceStageUHFEquiv_bijective`, and\n  `norm_sourceStageUHFEquiv` — each reports only `propext`,\n  `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder scan of the candidate and its direct P53/dyadic imports — no\n  `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`,\n  `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` occurrence.\n- Quarantine/live SHA-256 comparison and\n  `git diff --check -- AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicFiniteStageUHFBridge.lean`\n  — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding.  The review checked the multiplication order\nand all three convention-sensitive signs, the zero-coordinate and default\nfinite-enumeration cases, that the basis transport proves rather than assumes\nthe stage equivalence, and that the custom dyadic norm is explicitly defined\nthrough the constructed matrix model.  It also checked the packet's scope\nagainst P55B--P59: no forbidden downstream statement is present.  Compilation\nand axiom reports validate this finite conditional infrastructure only; they\ndo not validate P53's external coordinate hypotheses or any manuscript\nregional-algebra conclusion.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P55A candidate, the exact archive and its\nquarantine extraction, and this closeout review.  The repository already had\nmodified plan/task/decision files and numerous untracked candidates, packets,\nand reviews; they were not overwritten, reformatted, or otherwise changed.\nNo manuscript file was modified; no commit, push, dependency update, archive\nbuild, or dependency fetch occurred.\n# P55B closeout review — local-hyperbolic source/UHF bridge\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated infrastructure-only Lane-H scope; queue may\nadvance.**\n\nAristotle task `5b40a5f6-d59a-4281-b6db-b103e3692cfd` is terminal\n`COMPLETE` in\n`history/logs/20260808T174500Z-809ad1ae-tasks.log`.\nIts exact response archive\n`aristotle_responses/P55B-local-hyperbolic-source-uhf-bridge-809ad1ae-5b40a5f6.tar.gz`\nwas extracted only into\n`aristotle_responses/P55B-local-hyperbolic-source-uhf-bridge-809ad1ae-5b40a5f6-quarantine/`.\nNo build, update, or dependency fetch was run in that dependency-free\nsnapshot. Only the packet-authorized module\n`AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge.lean` was integrated into\nthe live project. Its live and quarantine SHA-256 values agree:\n\n```text\nf754604e0c6a1f870158f81cda06223a86364d0a461816b9e9e5e7c9f7261cad\n```\n\nThe archived P53 and P55A predecessor modules are byte-identical to their\nlocally integrated, audited counterparts (respectively\n`797dd652c0cef03fd6481aee5331446fdad4dba7f4db9f310bda6d6b76efcd1b`\nand\n`42b18ef984b2046a4004ae64e8e79a0df7454e0c122b8d9722145bc6e2d28b3a`).\nNo raw response record was integrated: the packet authorizes only this\ncandidate module; the archive and quarantine extraction remain raw evidence.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nThe module imports only the accepted P55A bridge and\n`Formalization.DyadicTensorTower`; through P55A it uses the accepted P53\nsource system. It adds no axiom, supplied coherent enumeration, supplied\ncommuting square, supplied cofinality, or supplied direct-limit equivalence.\nThe load-bearing declarations are:\n\n- `AlphaData.stageEnum`, `stageEnum_coherent`, and\n  `enumRepr_sourceIncl`: a constructed birth-stage/linear-order enumeration\n  of nested coordinate blocks, with old coordinates shifted exactly as the\n  dyadic embeddings require;\n- `stageUHFEquiv` and `stageUHFEquiv_sourceConnecting`: the P55A finite-stage\n  equivalences in those enumerations and their proved commuting square with\n  P53's `sourceConnecting`;\n- `CoordinateDyadicLimit`, `coordDyadicDirected`,\n  `sourceToCoordinateDyadic`, `sourceToCoordinateDyadic_of`, and\n  `sourceToCoordinateDyadic_unique`: the constructed coordinate dyadic limit,\n  the source-limit star equivalence, its canonical-stage formula, and\n  uniqueness from those formulas;\n- `stageCard_cofinal`, `coordinateDyadicUHFEquiv`, `sourceUHFEquiv`,\n  `sourceUHFEquiv_of`, and `sourceUHFEquiv_unique`: the infinite-coordinate\n  branch under `[Infinite I]`; and\n- `terminalStage`, `stageCard_eq_card`, `terminalDyadicEquiv`,\n  `sourceFiniteEquiv`, `sourceFiniteEquiv_of`, and\n  `sourceFiniteEquiv_unique`: the terminal finite-coordinate branch under\n  `[Finite I]`.\n\nThe module inherits precisely P53's explicit `AlphaData` premises: P52's\nlocally supported hyperbolic family and exhaustion, `[LinearOrder I]`, and\nthe auxiliary `symplectic` and `stage_surjective` fields. The new endpoint\nassumptions are explicit and disjoint: `[Infinite I]` for the cofinal-UHF\nequivalence, and `[Finite I]` for the terminal-stage finite equivalence.\nThey are not claims derived from the manuscript. P55B introduces no new\nmathematical premise beyond these branch typeclasses and does not weaken the\npacket target.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The coherent enumeration and the P55A/P53 commuting squares are constructed. They induce `sourceToCoordinateDyadic`. Under `[Infinite I]`, cofinal cardinalities give `sourceUHFEquiv : A.SourceLimit ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] QubitUHFAlgebra`; under `[Finite I]`, a terminal block gives `sourceFiniteEquiv : A.SourceLimit ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] QubitTensorPower (Nat.card I)`. The required canonical-stage formulas and uniqueness theorems are also proved. |\n| partial | This is infrastructure only. The result remains conditional on P53's named local-coordinate, symplecticity, and stage-surjectivity data. It neither constructs the manuscript's regional realization nor any analytic completion. |\n| blocked | None at the P55B gate. P55C's faithful concrete representations, P55D's C-star extension, and all P56--P59 state/GNS/factor/trace work remain downstream. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is met exactly at its stated conditional\nscope. The direct-limit route is an allowed project-local supporting theory:\nit changes no target and exposes every extra premise named above.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P55B, Lane H, as declared in the packet and `PLAN.md`.\n- **Predecessors:** only P53 and P55A. Both are locally integrated, compiled,\n  and semantically audited in\n  `reviews/P53-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha-closeout.md` and\n  `reviews/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-closeout.md`; the\n  archive proves they exactly match the live modules. No later P55C--P59\n  artifact is imported or used.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: constructed finite-stage coherence, the\n  source-to-coordinate-dyadic direct-limit equivalence, and separate\n  finite-terminal/infinite-cofinal endpoint equivalences.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected. The candidate does not construct\n  an operator-range or C-star completion, a regional C-star alpha, a state\n  identity, GNS tensor splitting, factor classification, or trace/weight.\n  Its only occurrences of those topics are negative scope statements in the\n  module documentation.\n\nNo manuscript clause is represented by this infrastructure-only packet. In\nparticular, it does not promote the still-unformalized short-range regional\nvon Neumann-algebra theorem.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge` — passed in\n  the live project (`8051/8051` jobs). No build ran in quarantine.\n- `lake build` — passed in the live project (already up to date, `0` jobs).\n- `lake env lean /dev/stdin` importing the candidate and printing axioms for\n  `stageEnum_coherent`, `enumRepr_sourceIncl`,\n  `stageUHFEquiv_sourceConnecting`, `sourceToCoordinateDyadic`,\n  `sourceToCoordinateDyadic_unique`, `stageCard_cofinal`,\n  `coordinateDyadicUHFEquiv`, `sourceUHFEquiv`,\n  `sourceUHFEquiv_unique`, `sourceFiniteEquiv`, and\n  `sourceFiniteEquiv_unique` — each reports only `propext`,\n  `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder/declaration scan across the candidate and direct P53/P55A/dyadic\n  imports — no `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`,\n  `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` occurrence.\n- Quarantine/live SHA-256 comparison and `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding. The review checked that the enumeration\norders coordinates by birth stage and pads old registers in the direction used\nby the dyadic connecting maps; that the coherence square is extended from\nPauli-word basis elements rather than assumed; that cofinality uses the\nexplicit `[Infinite I]` branch; and that the finite result reaches a terminal\ncoordinate block only under `[Finite I]`. It further checked that no\none-directional direct-limit property was used as an equivalence without the\ntwo inverse maps, and that no forbidden Lane-H conclusion leaked into code.\nCompilation and axiom reports validate this conditional algebraic\ninfrastructure; they do not establish P53's external coordinate hypotheses,\nany C-star completion, or any manuscript/operator-algebraic conclusion.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P55B candidate, its exact response\narchive, quarantine extraction, and this closeout review. The pre-existing\nmodified plan/task/decision files and unrelated untracked candidates, packets,\nand reviews were preserved. No manuscript file was modified; no commit, push,\ndependency update, archive build, or dependency fetch occurred.\n# P55C closeout review — local-hyperbolic concrete representations\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated conditional infrastructure-only Lane-H scope;\nqueue may advance.**\n\nAristotle task `7706fefb-a5b1-4939-a2d1-049e37cb3ddf` is terminal `COMPLETE`\nin `history/logs/20260808T183526Z-c0959aa3-tasks.log`.\nOnly its supplied exact archive,\n`aristotle_responses/P55C-local-hyperbolic-concrete-representations-c0959aa3-7706fefb.tar.gz`,\nwas extracted into\n`aristotle_responses/P55C-local-hyperbolic-concrete-representations-c0959aa3-7706fefb-quarantine/`.\nNo build, update, or dependency fetch ran in that dependency-free quarantine\nsnapshot. Only the packet-authorized module\n`AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicConcreteRepresentations.lean` was\nintegrated into the live project. The live and quarantine SHA-256 values agree:\n\n```text\n37d007ed52560bebc6e39173d1854bb15bba0bd1e6c7393457a40269880c3a8e\n```\n\nThe quarantined P53, P54, and P55B modules are byte-identical to their locally\nintegrated and audited predecessors, with SHA-256 values respectively\n`797dd652c0cef03fd6481aee5331446fdad4dba7f4db9f310bda6d6b76efcd1b`,\n`786a1b2b89bf14eb61cf7f703ea646d095d3d640ac20b814c012a6e82b1c8eb9`, and\n`f754604e0c6a1f870158f81cda06223a86364d0a461816b9e9e5e7c9f7261cad`.\nThe archive, quarantine extraction, and `ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md` remain raw\nresponse records; no other archive file or candidate module was copied.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nThe module imports only accepted P55B/P53 infrastructure, P54, and the local\n`ConcreteCStarCompletion` support module. It adds no axiom, supplied\nrepresentation, supplied completion, or supplied dense-range interface.\n\nThe reusable closed-range API is `ConcreteRange.rangeCStar`,\n`rangeEmbedding`, `rangeEmbedding_injective`, `rangeEmbedding_denseRange`,\n`rangeCStar_le`, `rangeCStar_isLeast`, and `rangeCStar_congr`. The closure is\nthe actual `StarSubalgebra.topologicalClosure` of the operator range in\nbounded operators, with its `IsClosed` and `CStarAlgebra` instances.\n\nFor `A : AlphaData L I`, the exact construction is:\n\n- `SourceConcreteRep`, containing only a source representation and its proved\n  injectivity;\n- `SourceConcreteRep.targetRep`, its transport through P53's `A.alpha.symm`,\n  with `targetRep_alpha` and `targetRep_injective`;\n- `sourceCStar`, `targetCStar`, `sourceEmbedding`, and `targetEmbedding`,\n  with injectivity and dense-range theorems;\n- `infiniteSourceRep` and `infiniteSourceRep_stage`, using P54's `uhfRep`\n  after P55B's `A.sourceUHFEquiv` under `[Infinite I]`;\n- `finiteSourceRep` and `finiteSourceRep_stage`, using P54's\n  `uhfStageRep (Nat.card I)` after P55B's `A.sourceFiniteEquiv` under\n  `[Finite I]`; and\n- `branchSourceRep`, `branchSourceRep_finite`, `branchSourceRep_infinite`,\n  `branchSourceEmbedding_injective_denseRange`, and\n  `branchTargetEmbedding_injective_denseRange`.\n\n`SourceConcreteRep.sourceNormedRing`, `sourceNormedAlgebra`, and\n`sourceCStarRing` additionally show that the norm pulled back from the\nfaithful representation satisfies the C-star identity. This is supporting\ninfrastructure; it assumes no norm preservation. The only premises beyond the\naccepted P53/P54/P55B data are the explicit finite/infinite branch\ntypeclasses. Thus P53's named local-coordinate, linear-order, `symplectic`,\nand `stage_surjective` assumptions remain inherited and external to the\nmanuscript.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | In the infinite branch, the constructed P54 representation is transported through P55B's source/UHF equivalence; in the finite branch, P54's terminal matrix representation is transported through P55B's terminal-stage equivalence. Both are faithful. The target representation is their transport through P53's algebraic `alpha.symm`. The two range closures are genuine C-star algebras with canonical injective, dense embeddings. |\n| partial | This remains infrastructure conditional on P53's explicit local-coordinate and surjectivity data. It creates concrete operator-range models of the P53 source and target limits, not the manuscript's state-dependent GNS/von Neumann algebra. |\n| blocked | No obstruction blocks the P55C gate. P55D's completed C-star alpha, P56's state identity, P57's spatial GNS tensor split, and P58--P59 factor/trace work remain downstream. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is met at its stated conditional scope. The\nroute uses P54's common `UHFGNS` representation space for both branches; this\nis an allowed project-local construction, and all additional premises are\nnamed above. The equality `targetCStar_eq_sourceCStar` is only equality of\nclosed operator ranges induced by the algebraic bijection. It neither exports\nnor proves the completed C-star extension reserved for P55D.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P55C, Lane H, as declared in the packet and `PLAN.md`.\n- **Predecessors:** P53, P54, and P55B are integrated, live-compiled, and\n  locally audited in their respective P53, P54, and P55B closeout reviews.\n  The exact quarantined copies match the live files by hash. No P55D--P59\n  artifact is imported or relied on.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged exactly: faithful source/regional algebraic\n  operator representations, closed operator-range C-star algebras, and\n  injective dense embeddings, with explicit finite and infinite branches.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected. The module does not state a\n  completed C-star alpha, product-state identity, GNS tensor factorization,\n  factor classification, or trace/weight theorem. Its sole occurrence of the\n  closure equality is documented as insufficient for the P55D extension.\n\nNo manuscript clause is claimed by this infrastructure-only package. In\nparticular, it does not establish the source-contract regional factor theorem\nat `main.tex:1740-1752`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.LocalHyperbolicConcreteRepresentations` —\n  passed in the live project (`8055/8055` jobs).\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.LocalHyperbolicConcreteRepresentations Formalization`\n  — passed in the live project (`8094` jobs).\n- `lake build` — passed in the live project (up to date, `0` jobs).\n- `lake env lean /dev/stdin` importing P55C and printing axioms for the\n  closed-range, finite/infinite branch, embedding, and non-vacuity\n  declarations — every checked declaration reports only `propext`,\n  `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder/declaration scan over P55C and direct P53/P54/P55B imports — no\n  `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or\n  `native_decide` occurrence.\n- Quarantine/live hash comparison and `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding. The review checked that both endpoint\nrepresentations are constructed from P54/P55B rather than supplied; the\ntarget faithfulness follows from a genuine algebraic equivalence; dense range\nis a closure theorem rather than an asserted interface; and the common-range\nequality is not silently promoted to a C-star extension. Lean compilation and\nthe axiom reports validate this conditional infrastructure only; they do not\nprove P53's external coordinate hypotheses, any state identity, spatial\nfactorization, factorhood, or manuscript theorem.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P55C candidate, the exact response archive\nand quarantine extraction, and this closeout review. The pre-existing modified\nplan/task/decision files and all unrelated untracked candidates, packets, and\nreviews were preserved. No manuscript file was modified; no commit, push,\ndependency update, archive build, or dependency fetch was performed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"co