{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba <original-home>/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | sed -n '325,336p'; nl -ba <original-home>/.codex/memories/rollout_summaries/2026-08-06T14-29-28-EPRR-two_lane_aristotle_autopilot_closeout_hardening.md | sed -n '38,64p'\"","aggregated_output":"   325\t## Reusable knowledge\n   326\t\n   327\t- The live runner is `work/aristotle_autopilot/aristotle_autopilot.py`, configured by `work/aristotle_autopilot/autopilot.toml`. It has independent finite-fiber FF15–FF23 and stabilizer-hyperfinite P37–P46 queues, one active Aristotle task per lane, Codex closeout only at terminal status, and advancement only after both machine-readable acceptance and decision fields. [Task 1]\n   328\t- Upload staging contains the Lean project, the three approved manuscript files, and `AUTONOMY_POLICY.md`; the policy forbids `sorry`, `admit`, axioms, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, and silent weakening. [Task 1]\n   329\t- The user systemd timer polls every five minutes. For NVM installation, the service and Python resolution need explicit `PATH` and `AUTOPILOT_CODEX_BIN=<original-home>/.nvm/versions/node/v24.14.0/bin/codex`; this run verified `codex-cli 0.146.0`. [Task 2]\n   330\t- Persist closeout metadata in `work/aristotle_autopilot/state.json` before starting Codex. An interrupted closeout without a machine-readable decision halts for review rather than retrying or advancing ambiguously. [Task 2]\n   331\t\n   332\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   333\t\n   334\t- symptom: systemd reports `[Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'codex'` and terminal Aristotle jobs never close out -> cause: the NVM executable is outside noninteractive PATH -> fix: set the absolute Codex path in both the service and runner, then verify the service environment. [Task 2]\n   335\t- symptom: a closeout consumes about 13 GB and clones/builds Mathlib -> cause: `lake build` was run in a stripped dow